<title>UK: Boots down on ex-dividend payout.</title>
<headline>Boots down on ex-dividend payout.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Boots Co Plc fell 27p to 667-1/2 in early trading on Thursday as the stock went ex-dividend as part of a special payout announced today.</p>
<p>The UK retailer said it would pay out 400.5 million stg  in a special dividend to shareholders as of June 4.</p>
<p>Boots also posted annual pre-tax pre-exceptional profits of 536.2 million stg, well within the range of analysts' estimates. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
